.TH GILLII 1 "2026-10-02" "gillii 0.1.0-dev" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
gillii \- locate and restore cached WeChat mini-program packages
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B gillii
.RI "list [--appid ID] [--root DIR]"
.br
.B gillii
.RI "clean [--appid ID] [--root DIR] [--dry-run]"
.br
.B gillii
.RI "info ID [--root DIR]"
.br
.B gillii
.RI "chase ID"
.br
.B gillii
.RI "setup | version | help [COMMAND] | completion bash|zsh|fish"
.SH DESCRIPTION
A Bash orchestration tool using Node.js 22+ for V1MMWX decryption,
main-package extraction, restoration and static verification.
This is an unpublished development build.
https://github.com/leo1394/homebrew-gillii
.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B list
Print only AppID and latest modification time, one row per AppID.
.TP
.B info
Show all cached packages for an AppID, including paths, versions, sizes,
modification times, cache roots and blocked paths.
.TP
.B clean
Permanently delete discovered .wxapkg files;
preserve other files and directories.
Quit WeChat first, then reopen only the target mini-program and run list.
Blocked paths or deletion errors cause a nonzero exit status.
.TP
.B setup
Copy bundled helpers to a user cache and install locked npm dependencies.
Requires npm registry access. Lifecycle scripts are disabled.
.TP
.B chase
Automatically select the newest readable main package, copy and restore it.
Install dependencies on first run; create ./ID-unique-suffix/source.
Failures preserve logs.
No business API requests are made.
.TP
.B completion
Print Bash, Zsh or Fish completion without runtime dependencies.
.TP
.B version, --version
Print exactly two metadata lines.
.TP
.B help, --help
Print help; command-specific help is also supported.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --appid ID
An identifier of the form wx followed by 16 lowercase hexadecimal digits.
.TP
.B --root DIR
Optional cache search directory for list, info or clean.
.TP
.B --dry-run
Preview AppIDs and latest modification times without deleting files.
.TP
.B --input FILE_OR_DIR
Optional package file or directory; select its newest readable main package.
.TP
.B --output NEWDIR
Optional new output directory; parent must exist.
.TP
.B --
End option parsing. These commands accept no positional operands afterward.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
gillii list
gillii info wx0123456789abcdef
gillii clean
gillii chase wx0123456789abcdef
gillii help chase
.fi
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B XDG_CACHE_HOME
Cache root, default $HOME/.cache.
.TP
.B GILLII_NODE
Node executable, default node.
.SH FILES
Output includes original.wxapkg, decrypted package, raw/, source/, logs/
and report.json. Dependencies are stored under the versioned user cache.
.SH CAVEATS
macOS privacy may block terminal reads. Copy the AppID directory with Finder
and use --input. AppID paths and timestamps cannot identify an app by name.
Cached subpackages from the same version are merged. Uncached pages are
listed in report.json with status complete_cached. Games are unsupported.
Original variable names,
server code and runtime equivalence cannot be recovered or guaranteed.
.SH EXIT STATUS
0 for success; 1 for invalid input, missing dependencies,
restoration or validation failure.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR bash (1),
.BR node (1)
